WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.043 --> 00:00:07.215
Citizens of Botica, it is my great
pleasure to welcome you on this...

00:00:07.298 --> 00:00:13.471
...the New Deal and the liberation of
the five kingdoms' 50th anniversary!

00:00:14.723 --> 00:00:16.474
Hail King Bulgher!

00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:18.893
And it is my greater pleasure...

00:00:18.977 --> 00:00:25.817
...to celebrate the birthday of my
beloved son and heir, Prince Kelby!

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:33.324
Highness, the prince cannot
be found. Begging your pardon.

00:00:33.658 --> 00:00:37.996
This is troublesome. Find the prince!

00:00:38.079 --> 00:00:39.748
As you wish.

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:46.713
A slight miscommunication.
Please, go on with your reveling!

00:00:52.177 --> 00:00:55.221
Come on, Sam.
The fireworks are starting!

00:00:55.346 --> 00:00:56.264
Right!

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:05.273
Now this is more like it.

00:01:05.356 --> 00:01:08.526
I've many fun
memories atop this old tree.

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:12.280
It’s a precious friend,
right next to you.

00:01:12.363 --> 00:01:14.866
That’s sweet of you to say.

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:19.079
But it's your birthday.
Shouldn't we return to the palace?

00:01:19.204 --> 00:01:21.956
King Bulgher must be worried.

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:26.753
I'm safe. We have our army,
Odin, and Gara’s Keep.

00:01:26.878 --> 00:01:27.879
Gara’s Keep?

00:01:27.962 --> 00:01:33.134
Right. I've never been there,
but it's an ancient stronghold.

00:01:33.218 --> 00:01:37.430
Odin says we would evacuate
there if we were attacked.

00:01:37.555 --> 00:01:41.810
Still, it’s nice the kingdom
is throwing such a grand party.

00:01:41.893 --> 00:01:46.731
It's a party for my father.
I wasn't born on the anniversary.

00:01:47.398 --> 00:01:53.238
"The day we conquered magic," etc.
It just celebrates the Botican ego.

00:01:53.738 --> 00:01:55.907
And your birthday.

00:01:56.449 --> 00:02:02.413
I’ll say this. I won't be my father.
I'll treasure family when I'm king.

00:02:02.914 --> 00:02:05.291
You mustn’t say that.

00:02:05.416 --> 00:02:10.421
King Bulgher is a glorious leader,
stalwart, brave, and true.

00:02:11.089 --> 00:02:14.259
You were created to think that, Sam.

00:02:14.342 --> 00:02:19.264
Anyway, I think spending the
holiday here with you is the best.

00:02:19.597 --> 00:02:23.268
Oh, that reminds me.
I made you a present!

00:02:23.601 --> 00:02:29.482
Wow, you didn’t have to do that.
Is that your programming too?

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:34.320
No, I did it because I wanted to.

00:02:35.363 --> 00:02:36.614
Wow...

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:42.120
This is wonderful! Thank you!

00:02:42.453 --> 00:02:44.706
Why are there two chains?

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:54.340
That’s perfect!
But pendant or no pendant...

00:02:54.465 --> 00:02:59.721
...let’s promise to always be
together no matter what, Sam.

00:03:00.305 --> 00:03:02.682
Yes, I promise!

